<title>SPAIN: Santander names ex-Argentaria head to board.</title>
<headline>Santander names ex-Argentaria head to board.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco de Santander said on Monday it has named the former chairman of Corporacion Bancaria de Espana (Argentaria) to its board of directors.</p>
<p>Francisco Luzon is to be joint-general director along with the president of Santander, and will also carry out strategy, communication and institutional relations duties, a note said.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
